# Strength, on a boulder inside Mt Coronet's first floor.
#
# Strength is the odd one: using it only ARMS the move, and the boulder moves
# when the player walks into it. So this station proves two things, the game
# recorded the move, and the player is standing on the tile the boulder was on.
#
# The tile north of the boulder has to be free for it to be pushed into, and
# free is not what the behavior byte says: the first boulder tried here had
# behavior 00 on both sides and solid collision on both, so Strength was used,
# the walk was refused and the station passed its journal assert while proving
# nothing. The port's map scan reports collision beside behavior for that
# reason, and this boulder was picked from it.

name PUSHER
gender GENDER_MALE
trainer-id 30003
money 3000
badge BADGE_ID_MINE
party SPECIES_BIBAREL 30 ITEM_NONE
party-move 0 0 MOVE_STRENGTH
map MAP_HEADER_MT_CORONET_1F_NORTH_ROOM_1 18 44 FACE_UP
